        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{2}{3} x \\,\\textrm d x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Calculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{2}{3} x \\,\\textrm d x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222b(2)/(3)xdx|= (2)/(3)\u222bxdx; = (2)/(3)((x^{1 + 1})/(1 + 1)) + C; = (2)/(3) \u22c5 (x^{2})/(2) + C; = (1)/(3)x^{2} + C]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n[MATH: \u222b(2)/(3)xdx|= (2)/(3)\u222bxdx; = (2)/(3)((x^{1 + 1})/(1 + 1)) + C; = (2)/(3) \u22c5 (x^{2})/(2) + C; = (1)/(3)x^{2} + C]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{2}{3} x \\,\\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n[MATH: \u222b(2)/(3)xdx|= (2)/(3)\u222bxdx; = (2)/(3)((x^{1 + 1})/(1 + 1)) + C; = (2)/(3) \u22c5 (x^{2})/(2) + C; = (1)/(3)x^{2} + C]"
      },
