        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int 6 \\,\\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n[MATH: \u222b6dx|= 6\u222b1dx; = 6\u222bx^{0}dx; = 6 \u22c5 (x^{0 + 1})/(0 + 1) + C; = 6 \u22c5 x + C; = 6x + C]\n\nIn general, we can see that for any constant [MATH: k,] we have [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int k \\,\\textrm d x = kx + C.]"
